{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat ../research.json'","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"audit_spec_path\": \"/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-09-28_18-02-29-hashicorp_raft-real-run/audit-spec/v1.json\",\n  \"audit_spec_version\": 1,\n  \"activity_roles\": {\n    \"A1\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Qualified support for decision formation and legal advancement\"\n    },\n    \"A2\": {\n      \"role\": \"core\",\n      \"relation\": \"Context validity and acquisition, transfer or loss of authority\"\n    },\n    \"A3\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Recovery and resynchronization of eligible participation\"\n    },\n    \"A4\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Configuration and participant eligibility\"\n    },\n    \"A5\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Decision application and consumption\"\n    },\n    \"A6\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"History, persistence and reconstruction of support\"\n    },\n    \"A7\": {\n      \"role\": \"support\",\n      \"relation\": \"Client contracts, invocation intervals and observed completion\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"activity_focus\": [],\n  \"understanding_status\": \"usable\",\n  \"core_overview\": {\n    \"formation\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"ApplyLog creates a command future and sends applyCh. The leader main loop rejects transfer/removal cases or assigns term/index and stores a batch. Successful local storage and successful per-peer append/snapshot paths report indices into the leader-generation commitment. Only current voter slots count; the majority index must reach the first index of this leader term. The commit notification makes the leader record commitIndex, commit configuration changes and enqueue indexed work to processLogs/runFSM. Replication requests propagate LeaderCommitIndex; followers validate previous entries, reconcile/store suffixes and apply the bounded leader commit. FSM return precedes local command future response. Heartbeats omit entries and commit index, and are not log support.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"b-admit\",\n        \"b-dispatch\",\n        \"b-append\",\n        \"b-replicate\",\n        \"b-commit\",\n        \"b-consume-commit\",\n        \"b-fsm\",\n        \"b-install\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"f-append-accepted\",\n        \"f-match\",\n        \"f-commit\",\n        \"f-fsm-queued\",\n        \"f-applied\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-apply\",\n        \"s-commitment\",\n        \"s-dispatch\",\n        \"s-election\",\n        \"s-follower\",\n        \"s-fsm\",\n        \"s-future-completion\",\n        \"s-future-contract\",\n        \"s-inmem-heartbeat\",\n        \"s-inmem-pipeline\",\n        \"s-install\",\n        \"s-leader-life\",\n        \"s-leader-loop\",\n        \"s-match-notify\",\n        \"s-network-dispatch\",\n        \"s-network-pipeline\",\n        \"s-pipeline\",\n        \"s-repl-ownership\",\n        \"s-replication\",\n        \"s-rpc\",\n        \"s-snapshot-send\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"context\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"A timed-out eligible follower becomes candidate; optional pre-vote precedes a real campaign that persists a new term/self vote and asks configured voters. RequestVote checks membership, known leader, term, saved vote and last-entry freshness. Campaign-local channels isolate old replies. Majority selects Leader; setup creates a fresh commitment object and no-op. Higher-term RPC/reply handling, insufficient recent voter contact, negative verification or committed self removal can demote. Leader exit closes worker stop channels and fails unresolved local futures; captured worker support remains attached to the old object. Transfer waits for target replication and sends TimeoutNow, whose candidate bypasses pre-vote but still seeks real votes. Restart restores term/history/configuration as Follower. Network empty-heartbeat handling can bypass the main RPC queue; it is an actual asynchronous owner, despite main-thread-only comments.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"b-vote\",\n        \"b-campaign\",\n        \"b-leader-life\",\n        \"b-heartbeat\",\n        \"b-lease\",\n        \"b-verify\",\n        \"b-recover\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"f-vote-granted\",\n        \"f-leader-generation\",\n        \"f-contact\",\n        \"f-verification-notification\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-bootstrap\",\n        \"s-campaign\",\n        \"s-election\",\n        \"s-follower\",\n        \"s-heartbeat\",\n        \"s-inmem-heartbeat\",\n        \"s-leader-life\",\n        \"s-leader-loop\",\n        \"s-match-notify\",\n        \"s-network-dispatch\",\n        \"s-prevote\",\n        \"s-repl-ownership\",\n        \"s-replication\",\n        \"s-rpc\",\n        \"s-stable-context\",\n        \"s-startup\",\n        \"s-timeout-config\",\n        \"s-transfer\",\n        \"s-verify-api\",\n        \"s-verify-vote\",\n        \"s-vote\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"connection\": {\n      \"explanation\": \"Log and snapshot history survive role changes, while volatile support and client futures do not transfer to a new leader generation. New authority re-establishes index support through real replication and its current-term no-op; voter log-freshness checks connect persisted history to elections. Membership is latest-versus-committed: new leader changes wait for a committed current-term entry and stable configuration, then update voter aggregation and all-peer replication; retained voter IDs preserve their slots. Followers roll back latest configuration on suffix conflict and recover configuration from snapshot/logs. Snapshot installation supplies a prefix match only after storage/FSM restore and response processing; application queueing is distinct from completed application. VerifyLeader uses a separate Boolean notification path and must not be equated with commitment. User Restore is an explicitly restricted disaster-recovery override with aborted inflight futures and a later no-op completion.\",\n      \"behavior_ids\": [\n        \"b-leader-life\",\n        \"b-config\",\n        \"b-vote\",\n        \"b-recover\",\n        \"b-install\",\n        \"b-user-restore\",\n        \"b-verify\"\n      ],\n      \"fact_ids\": [\n        \"f-match\",\n        \"f-vote-granted\",\n        \"f-verification-notification\"\n      ],\n      \"source_ids\": [\n        \"s-bootstrap\",\n        \"s-commitment\",\n        \"s-config-change\",\n        \"s-dispatch\",\n        \"s-fsm\",\n        \"s-heartbeat\",\n        \"s-install\",\n        \"s-leader-life\",\n        \"s-leader-loop\",\n        \"s-match-notify\",\n        \"s-membership-contract\",\n        \"s-repl-ownership\",\n        \"s-replication\",\n        \"s-restore-contract\",\n        \"s-rpc\",\n        \"s-snapshot-send\",\n        \"s-stable-context\",\n        \"s-startup\",\n        \"s-transfer\",\n        \"s-user-restore\",\n        \"s-verify-api\",\n        \"s-verify-vote\",\n        \"s-vote\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"open_details\": [\n      \"Network heartbeat concurrent context-write interleavings versus main loop; source comments and wiring differ.\",\n      \"VerifyLeader suffrage filtering, response timing and applicable authority contract need discrimination.\",\n      \"Heartbeat contact versus higher-term reply handling: other workers and negative verification may protect authority.\",\n      \"Pipeline error/partial-response semantics relative to AppendFuture.Response contract.\",\n      \"Automatic snapshot creation/compaction, forced RecoverCluster and store-specific crash behavior remain deferred.\",\n      \"No executed operation history, property evidence, or overall correctness conclusion exists.\"\n    ],\n    \"core_gaps\": [],\n    \"status\": \"usable\",\n   