committed.\"\n            ],\n            \"async_boundaries\": [],\n            \"produces_fact_ids\": [],\n            \"consumes_fact_ids\": [],\n            \"cross_activity_effects\": {\n              \"A1\": \"Latest voter membership defines which match slots participate in majority.\",\n              \"A2\": \"Latest voter membership controls elections and lease; committed local removal leads to step-down.\"\n            },\n            \"existing_protections\": [],\n            \"source_ids\": [\n              \"s-repl-ownership\",\n              \"s-dispatch\",\n              \"s-rpc\",\n              \"s-config-change\",\n              \"s-membership-contract\"\n            ],\n            \"unknowns\": []\n          }\n        },\n        \"b-consume-commit\": {\n          \"before\": {},\n          \"after\": {\n            \"id\": \"b-consume-commit\",\n            \"primary_activity\": \"A5\",\n            \"execution_owner\": \"Leader main loop or follower appendEntries -> processLogs\",\n            \"protocol_context\": \"Log indices after lastApplied through committed bound\",\n            \"trigger\": \"Commit notification or advancing LeaderCommitIndex\",\n            \"legal_preconditions\": [],\n            \"implementation_guards\": [],\n            \"reads\": [],\n            \"writes\": [\n              \"Leader records commitIndex, marks configuration committed and associates inflight futures by log index. processLogs retrieves prior entries and queues command/barrier/config tuples.\"\n            ],\n            \"durable_effects\": [],\n            \"external_effects\": [],\n            \"important_branches\": [\n              \"Old indices skipped; log read error panics; shutdown responds with error. Noops bypass FSM. Self removal takes effect after committed work is enqueued.\"\n            ],\n            \"async_boundaries\": [\n              \"lastApplied advances after enqueue; it does not prove FSM.Apply returned.\"\n            ],\n            \"produces_fact_ids\": [\n              \"f-fsm-queued\"\n            ],\n            \"consumes_fact_ids\": [\n              \"f-commit\"\n            ],\n            \"cross_activity_effects\": {\n              \"A7\": \"Future accompanies its indexed command into FSM worker; queue admission alone does not complete it.\"\n            },\n            \"existing_protections\": [],\n            \"source_ids\": [\n              \"s-leader-loop\",\n              \"s-dispatch\",\n              \"s-rpc\"\n            ],\n            \"unknowns\": []\n          }\n        },\n        \"b-dispatch\": {\n          \"before\": {},\n          \"after\": {\n            \"id\": \"b-dispatch\",\n            \"primary_activity\": \"A6\",\n            \"execution_owner\": \"Leader main loop: dispatchLogs\",\n            \"protocol_context\": \"Current leader term and fresh leaderState.commitment\",\n            \"trigger\": \"Leader batches applies or emits initial no-op\",\n            \"legal_preconditions\": [],\n            \"implementation_guards\": [],\n            \"reads\": [],\n            \"writes\": [\n              \"Assign increasing Index and current Term; put futures in inflight.\"\n            ],\n            \"durable_effects\": [\n              \"Call LogStore.StoreLogs before matching localID or updating lastLog. Durability depends on selected store.\"\n            ],\n            \"external_effects\": [],\n            \"important_branches\": [\n              \"Store error responds to futures and sets Follower; it does not call match.\"\n            ],\n            \"async_boundaries\": [],\n            \"produces_fact_ids\": [\n              \"f-match\"\n            ],\n            \"consumes_fact_ids\": [],\n            \"cross_activity_effects\": {\n              \"A1\": \"Successful local storage contributes one eligible voter match index.\"\n            },\n            \"existing_protections\": [],\n            \"source_ids\": [\n              \"s-dispatch\",\n              \"s-leader-life\"\n            ],\n            \"unknowns\": []\n          }\n        },\n        \"b-fsm\": {\n          \"before\": {},\n          \"after\": {\n            \"id\": \"b-fsm\",\n            \"primary_activity\": \"A5\",\n            \"execution_owner\": \"runFSM goroutine\",\n            \"protocol_context\": \"Ordered commit tuples with optional logFuture; injected FSM implementation\",\n            \"trigger\": \"fsmMutateCh work\",\n            \"legal_preconditions\": [],\n            \"implementation_guards\": [],\n            \"reads\": [],\n            \"writes\": [],\n            \"durable_effects\": [],\n            \"external_effects\": [\n              \"Invoke FSM.Apply or ApplyBatch; save response on future and respond nil afterwards.\"\n            ],\n            \"important_branches\": [\n              \"Batching requires response count equal sent commands/configurations; mismatch panics. Barrier not sent to ApplyBatch. Optional ConfigurationStore receives configurations on single path. Restore opens snapshot, invokes FSM restore then completes restoreFuture.\"\n            ],\n            \"async_boundaries\": [],\n            \"produces_fact_ids\": [\n              \"f-applied\"\n            ],\n            \"consumes_fact_ids\": [\n              \"f-fsm-queued\"\n            ],\n            \"cross_activity_effects\": {\n              \"A7\": \"Error completion synchronizes access to FSM response; application-returned errors are Response values, separate from Raft Error.\"\n            },\n            \"existing_protections\": [],\n            \"source_ids\": [\n              \"s-fsm\",\n              \"s-future-completion\",\n              \"s-future-contract\"\n            ],\n            \"unknowns\": []\n          }\n        },\n        \"b-heartbeat\": {\n          \"before\": {},\n          \"after\": {\n            \"id\": \"b-heartbeat\",\n            \"primary_activity\": \"A2\",\n            \"execution_owner\": \"Independent per-peer heartbeat goroutine\",\n            \"protocol_context\": \"Captured replication term, peer, shared LastContact and pending verification notifications\",\n            \"trigger\": \"Periodic interval or notifyCh\",\n            \"legal_preconditions\": [],\n            \"implementation_guards\": [],\n            \"reads\": [],\n            \"writes\": [\n              \"On transport success update contact timestamp and call notifyAll(resp.Success).\"\n            ],\n            \"durable_effects\": [],\n            \"external_effects\": [],\n            \"important_branches\": [\n              \"Transport errors back off and do not update contact; response Term is not inspected here. Negative Success submits negative verification support.\"\n            ],\n            \"async_boundaries\": [\n              \"Runs independently of blocked ordinary replication. Network transport dispatches structurally empty heartbeats directly; in-memory transport queues them.\"\n            ],\n            \"produces_fact_ids\": [\n              \"f-contact\",\n              \"f-verification-notification\"\n            ],\n            \"consumes_fact_ids\": [],\n            \"cross_activity_effects\": {},\n            \"existing_protections\": [\n              \"Higher-term rejection from appendEntries gives Success=false; pending verification may then force step-down. Ordinary replication and lease still run.\"\n            ],\n            \"source_ids\": [\n              \"s-heartbeat\",\n              \"s-replication\",\n              \"s-rpc\",\n              \"s-network-dispatch\",\n              \"s-inmem-heartbeat\"\n            ],\n            \"unknowns\": []\n          }\n        },\n        \"b-install\": {\n          \"before\": {},\n          \"after\": {\n            \"id\": \"b-install\",\n            \"primary_activity\": \"A3\",\n            \"execution_owner\": \"Snapshot sender replication worker, receiver main loop and FSM restore worker\",\n            \"protocol_context\": \"Captured leader term, snapshot index/term and configuration\",\n            \"trigger\": \"Missing log on replication -> sendLatestSnapshot -> InstallSnapshot\",\n            \"legal_preconditions\": [],\n            \"implementation_guards\": [\n              \"Receiver validates version and rejects old term; adopts higher term. Checks transferred length, closes sink, waits for FSM restore. Sender rejects higher reply term and matches only on Success.\"\n            ],\n            \"reads\": [],\n            \"writes\": [\n              \"Receiver updates lastApplied, lastSnapshot and both configurations; compacts/removes logs. Sender sets nextIndex=meta.Index+1 and matches captured peer ID.\"\n            ],\n            \"durable_effects\": [],\n            \"external_effects\": [],\n            \"important_branches\": [\n              \"Copy, sink and FSM errors reject. Post-restore compaction errors are logged but success remains possible.\"\n            ],\n            \"async_boundaries\": [],\n            \"produces_fact_ids\": [\n              \"f-match\"\n            ],\n            \"consumes_fact_ids\": [],\n            \"cross_activity_effects\": {\n              \"A1\": \"Successful snapshot reply contributes snapshot index to same leader commitment object.\",\n              \"A2\": \"Snapshot request carries context term and establishes recovered participation metadata.\"\n            },\n            \"existing_protections\": [],\n            \"source_ids\": [\n              \"s-snapshot-send\",\n              \"s-install\",\n              \"s-fsm\"\n            ],\n            \"unknowns\": []\n          }\n        },\n        \"b-leader-life\": {\n          \"before\": {},\n          \"after\": {\n            \"id\": \"b-leader-life\",\n            \"primary_activity\": \"A2\",\n            \"execution_owner\": \"runLeader setup and deferred cleanup; leaderLoop\",\n            \"protocol_context\": \"A new leaderState generation with first new index = getLastIndex()+1\",\n            \"trigger\": \"Enter or leave Leader role\",\n            \"legal_preconditions\": [],\n            \"implementation_guards\": [],\n            \"reads\": [],\n            \"writes\": [\n              \"Fresh commitment/inflight/replState/notification/stepDown objects. Start workers and dispatch initial noop.\"\n            ],\n            \"durable_effects\": [],\n            \"external_effects\": [],\n            \"important_branches\": [\n              \"On exit close peer stop channels, fail inflight and pending verification futures with ErrLeadershipLost, clear generation state. Higher-term replication signal, incoming RPC, lease failure or committed self removal can cause exit.\"\n            ],\n            \"async_boundaries\": [],\n            \"produces_fact_ids\": [],\n            \"consumes_fact_ids\": [\n              \"f-leader-generation\"\n            ],\n            \"cross_activity_effects\": {\n              \"A1\": \"Prior stored entries can be committed under new leader after current-term support is re-established.\",\n              \"A7\": \"Leadership loss fails pending futures without proving writes absent from future history.\"\n            },\n            \"existing_protections\": [\n              \"New commitment starts with zero matches and current-term threshold. Stored old entries survive; late worker matches update old object.\",\n              \"Lease counts recent contact only for latest voters; it is not a read lease contract.\"\n            ],\n            \"source_ids\": [\n              \"s-leader-life\",\n              \"s-leader-loop\",\n              \"s-repl-ownership\",\n              \"s-transfer\",\n              \"s-match-notify\"\n            ],\n            \"unknowns\": []\n          }\n        },\n        \"b-lease\": {\n          \"before\": {},\n          \"after\": {\n            \"id\": \"b-lease\",\n            \"primary_activity\": \"A2\",\n            \"execution_owner\": \"Leader main loop: checkLeaderLease\",\n            \"protocol_context\": \"Latest voter set, peer contact timestamps and LeaderLeaseTimeout\",\n            \"trigger\": \"Lease timer\",\n            \"legal_preconditions\": [],\n            \"implementation_guards\": [\n              \"Counts only voters including local self; if contacted count below voter majority set Follower.\"\n            ],\n            \"reads\": [],\n            \"writes\": [],\n            \"durable_effects\": [],\n            \"external_effects\": [],\n            \"important_branches\": [],\n            \"async_boundaries\": [],\n            \"produces_fact_ids\": [],\n            \"consumes_fact_ids\": [\n              \"f-contact\"\n            ],\n            \"cross_activity_effects\": {},\n            \"existing_protections\": [],\n            \"source_ids\": [\n              \"s-transfer\",\n              \"s-leader-loop\"\n            ],\n            \"unknowns\": [\n              \"Contact timestamp establishes transport response receipt, not successful acknowledgment of current authority. Whether this distinction permits a relevant bad endpoint needs a controlled schedule.\"\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        \"b-notify-replication\": {\n          \"before\": {},\n          \"after\": {\n            \"id\": \"b-notify-replication\",\n            \"primary_activity\": \"A2\",\n            \"execution_owner\": \"Successful replication or snapshot worker; handleStaleTerm\",\n            \"protocol_context\": \"Per-worker pending verification map\",\n            \"trigger\": \"Successful append/snapshot or higher-term reply\",\n            \"legal_preconditions\": [],\n            \"implementation_guards\": [],\n            \"reads\": [],\n            \"writes\": [\n              \"notifyAll swaps out pending map under lock and calls vote once per registered future. Successful append/snapshot notifies true; stale term notifies false and signals stepDown.\"\n            ],\n            \"durable_effects\": [],\n            \"external_effects\": [],\n            \"important_branches\": [],\n            \"async_boundaries\": [],\n            \"produces_fact_ids\": [\n              \"f-verification-notification\"\n            ],\n            \"consumes_fact_ids\": [],\n            \"cross_activity_effects\": {},\n            \"existing_protections\": [\n              \"Per-worker map draining prevents repeated notification of same registration.\"\n            ],\n            \"source_ids\": [\n              \"s-match-notify\",\n              \"s-snapshot-send\",\n              \"s-replication\"\n            ],\n            \"unknowns\": []\n          }\n        },\n        \"b-recover\": {\n          \"before\": {},\n          \"after\": {\n            \"id\": \"b-recover\",\n            \"primary_activity\": \"A3\",\n            \"execution_owner\": \"NewRaft initialization before starting workers\",\n            \"protocol_context\": \"Stable term, log suffix and chosen snapshot\",\n            \"trigger\": \"Construct/restart Raft\",\n            \"legal_preconditions\": [],\n            \"implementation_guards\": [],\n            \"reads\": [],\n            \"writes\": [\n              \"Initialize Follower, load stable term and last log, restore first usable snapshot, initialize snapshot/configuration metadata, scan remaining logs for configurations.\"\n            ],\n            \"durable_effects\": [],\n            \"external_effects\": [],\n            \"important_branches\": [\n              \"Snapshot restore failure tries older snapshots; if none usable construction fails. NoSnapshotRestoreOnStart skips FSM restore but accepts metadata. Bootstrap rejects existing state and stores term 1/config log 1.\"\n            ],\n            \"async_boundaries\": [],\n            \"produces_fact_ids\": [],\n            \"consumes_fact_ids\": [],\n            \"cross_activity_effects\": {\n              \"A1\": \"Recovered log and snapshot boundaries supply future replication and vote freshness.\",\n              \"A2\": \"Volatile leader authority is not restored; loaded term/configuration constrain fresh election.\"\n            },\n            \"existing_protections\": [],\n            \"source_ids\": [\n              \"s-startup\",\n              \"s-bootstrap\",\n              \"s-rpc\"\n            ],\n            \"unknowns\": [\n              \"Backend persistence guarantees, automatic snapshot production/compaction and forced RecoverCluster internals are not mapped.\"\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        \"b-replicate\": {\n          \"before\": {},\n          \"after\": {\n            \"id\": \"b-replicate\",\n            \"primary_activity\": \"A1\",\n            \"execution_owner\": \"Per-peer replication worker and pipeline decoder\",\n            \"protocol_context\": \"Captured followerReplication.currentTerm, peer ID, commitment object, request entries\",\n            \"trigger\": \"Trigger, CommitTimeout or pipeline completion\",\n            \"legal_preconditions\": [],\n            \"implementation_guards\": [\n              \"Ordinary RPC transport error does not match. Higher reply term invokes handleStaleTerm and stops. Successful nonempty reply matches last request entry.\"\n            ],\n            \"reads\": [],\n            \"writes\": [],\n            \"durable_effects\": [],\n            \"external_effects\": [],\n            \"important_branches\": [\n              \"Reject backs off nextIndex; missing log invokes snapshot fallback; successful sync enables pipeline. Pipeline checks Term and Success but does not call ready.Error before reading Response.\"\n            ],\n            \"async_boundaries\": [\n              \"Captured commitment and stepDown channels belong to one leaderState generation.\",\n              \"Pipeline producer completes futures including error cases before publishing them.\"\n            ],\n            \"produces_fact_ids\": [\n              \"f-match\"\n            ],\n            \"consumes_fact_ids\": [\n              \"f-append-accepted\"\n            ],\n            \"cross_activity_effects\": {},\n            \"existing_protections\": [\n              \"Old workers retain old commitment object rather than attaching support to a later leader generation.\"\n            ],\n            \"source_ids\": [\n              \"s-replication\",\n              \"s-pipeline\",\n              \"s-match-notify\",\n              \"s-repl-ownership\",\n              \"s-network-pipeline\",\n              \"s-inmem-pipeline\"\n            ],\n            \"unknowns\": [\n              \"Whether a transport error can leave an apparently successful pipeline Response requires actual decoding/error analysis.\"\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        \"b-user-restore\": {\n          \"before\": {},\n          \"after\": {\n            \"id\": \"b-user-restore\",\n            \"primary_activity\": \"A3\",\n            \"execution_owner\": \"Leader restoreUserSnapshot and public Restore wrapper\",\n            \"protocol_context\": \"Disaster-recovery operation with stable latest configuration\",\n            \"trigger\": \"User Restore request\",\n            \"legal_preconditions\": [],\n            \"implementation_guards\": [],\n            \"reads\": [],\n            \"writes\": [\n              \"Abort inflight operations, use current config and term, burn index beyond both current log and supplied snapshot, create and restore snapshot. Public wrapper subsequently waits for noop through applyCh.\"\n            ],\n            \"durable_effects\": [],\n            \"external_effects\": [],\n            \"important_branches\": [\n              \"Reject unstable configuration and unsupported version; snapshot/FSM failures handled separately. API explicitly restricts intended use to disaster recovery into a fresh cluster.\"\n            ],\n            \"async_boundaries\": [],\n            \"produces_fact_ids\": [],\n            \"consumes_fact_ids\": [],\n            \"cross_activity_effects\": {\n              \"A1\": \"Burned log hole drives followers to snapshot fallback; subsequent no-op waits for replication.\",\n              \"A7\": \"Inflight errors are ErrAbortedByRestore; public Restore completion includes later noop.\"\n            },\n            \"existing_protections\": [],\n            \"source_ids\": [\n              \"s-user-restore\",\n              \"s-restore-contract\"\n            ],\n            \"unknowns\": []\n          }\n        },\n        \"b-verify\": {\n          \"before\": {},\n          \"after\": {\n            \"id\": \"b-verify\",\n            \"primary_activity\": \"A2\",\n            \"execution_owner\": \"verifyLeader registration; verifyFuture.vote; leaderLoop result consumer\",\n            \"protocol_context\": \"Future object, captured voter-majority threshold, replication-worker registrations\",\n            \"trigger\": \"Public VerifyLeader enqueues future\",\n            \"legal_preconditions\": [],\n            \"implementation_guards\": [],\n            \"reads\": [],\n            \"writes\": [\n              \"Initialize self vote and voter quorum threshold; register future with all replState workers; first negative or enough positive votes re-enqueues future. LeaderLoop responds success if tally meets threshold, otherwise demotes and returns ErrNotLeader.\"\n            ],\n            \"durable_effects\": [],\n            \"external_effects\": [],\n            \"important_branches\": [\n              \"Single-voter threshold completes immediately; registrations do not filter Suffrage. Vote lock and nil notifyCh prevent multiple final notifications. Leader cleanup fails pending verification on exit.\"\n            ],\n            \"async_boundaries\": [],\n            \"produces_fact_ids\": [],\n            \"consumes_fact_ids\": [\n              \"f-verification-notification\"\n            ],\n            \"cross_activity_effects\": {\n              \"A7\": \"Successful public verification may be used by caller to avoid serving stale FSM data, per API comment.\"\n            },\n            \"existing_protections\": [],\n            \"source_ids\": [\n              \"s-verify-api\",\n              \"s-leader-loop\",\n              \"s-verify-vote\",\n              \"s-repl-ownership\"\n            ],\n            \"unknowns\": [\n              \"Need distinguish intended authority guarantee from nonvoter contributions. No observed public completion or stale application read is claimed.\"\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        \"b-vote\": {\n          \"before\": {},\n          \"after\": {\n            \"id\": \"b-vote\",\n            \"primary_activity\": \"A2\",\n            \"execution_owner\": \"requestVote RPC receiver\",\n            \"protocol_context\": \"Candidate address/ID, request term, local latest configuration and last entry\",\n            \"trigger\": \"RequestVote delivered\",\n            \"legal_preconditions\": [],\n            \"implementation_guards\": [\n              \"Reject unknown candidate ID when configuration nonempty; reject competing known leader unless transfer; reject old term; reject nonvoter candidate; compare last log term then index.\"\n            ],\n            \"reads\": [],\n            \"writes\": [],\n            \"durable_effects\": [\n              \"Adopt higher term through stable store. Persist vote term then candidate bytes before granting new vote.\"\n            ],\n            \"external_effects\": [],\n            \"important_branches\": [\n              \"Duplicate same-term vote grants only matching candidate bytes; it returns before freshness comparison. Storage read/write errors reject; current-term persistence failure panics.\"\n            ],\n            \"async_boundaries\": [],\n            \"produces_fact_ids\": [\n              \"f-vote-granted\"\n            ],\n            \"consumes_fact_ids\": [],\n            \"cross_activity_effects\": {},\n            \"existing_protections\": [\n              \"Persistent per-term candidate selection and log freshness checks.\"\n            ],\n            \"source_ids\": [\n              \"s-vote\",\n              \"s-stable-context\"\n            ],\n            \"unknowns\": [\n              \"Two separate vote writes: partial-failure/recovery contract of selected StableStore remains to be investigated.\"\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        \"core_overview\": {\n          \"before\": {},\n          \"after\": {\n            \"formation\": {\n              \"explanation\": \"ApplyLog creates a command future and sends applyCh. The leader main loop rejects transfer/removal cases or assigns term/index and stores a batch. Successful local storage and successful per-peer append/snapshot paths report indices into the leader-generation commitment. Only current voter slots count; the majority index must reach the first index of this leader term. The commit notification makes the leader record commitIndex, commit configuration changes and enqueue indexed work to processLogs/runFSM. Replication requests propagate LeaderCommitIndex; followers validate previous entries, reconcile/store suffixes and apply the bounded leader commit. FSM return precedes local command future response. Heartbeats omit entries and commit index, and are not log support.\",\n              \"behavior_ids\": [\n                \"b-admit\",\n                \"b-dispatch\",\n                \"b-append\",\n                \"b-replicate\",\n                \"b-commit\",\n                \"b-consume-commit\",\n                \"b-fsm\",\n                \"b-install\"\n              ],\n              \"fact_ids\": [\n                \"f-append-accepted\",\n                \"f-match\",\n                \"f-commit\",\n                \"f-fsm-queued\",\n                \"f-applied\"\n              ],\n              \"source_ids\": [\n                \"s-apply\",\n                \"s-commitment\",\n                \"s-dispatch\",\n                \"s-election\",\n                \"s-follower\",\n                \"s-fsm\",\n                \"s-future-completion\",\n                \"s-future-contract\",\n                \"s-inmem-heartbeat\",\n                \"s-inmem-pipeline\",\n                \"s-install\",\n                \"s-leader-life\",\n                \"s-leader-loop\",\n                \"s-match-notify\",\n                \"s-network-dispatch\",\n                \"s-network-pipeline\",\n                \"s-pipeline\",\n                \"s-repl-ownership\",\n                \"s-replication\",\n                \"s-rpc\",\n                \"s-snapshot-send\"\n              ]\n            },\n            \"context\": {\n              \"explanation\": \"A timed-out eligible follower becomes candidate; optional pre-vote precedes a real campaign that persists a new term/self vote and asks configured voters. RequestVote checks membership, known leader, term, saved vote and last-entry freshness. Campaign-local channels isolate old replies. Majority selects Leader; setup creates a fresh commitment object and no-op. Higher-term RPC/reply handling, insufficient recent voter contact, negative verification or committed self removal can demote. Leader exit closes worker stop channels and fails unresolved local futures; captured worker support remains attached to the old object. Transfer waits for target replication and sends TimeoutNow, whose candidate bypasses pre-vote but still seeks real votes. Restart restores term/history/configuration as Follower. Network empty-heartbeat handling can bypass the main RPC queue; it is an actual asynchronous owner, despite main-thread-only comments.\",\n              \"behavior_ids\": [\n                \"b-vote\",\n                \"b-campaign\",\n                \"b-leader-life\",\n                \"b-heartbeat\",\n                \"b-lease\",\n                \"b-verify\",\n                \"b-recover\"\n              ],\n              \"fact_ids\": [\n                \"f-vote-granted\",\n                \"f-leader-generation\",\n                \"f-contact\",\n                \"f-verification-notification\"\n              ],\n              \"source_ids\": [\n                \"s-bootstrap\",\n                \"s-campaign\",\n                \"s-election\",\n                \"s-follower\",\n                \"s-heartbeat\",\n                \"s-inmem-heartbeat\",\n                \"s-leader-life\",\n                \"s-leader-loop\",\n                \"s-match-notify\",\n                \"s-network-dispatch\",\n                \"s-prevote\",\n                \"s-repl-ownership\",\n                \"s-replication\",\n                \"s-rpc\",\n                \"s-stable-context\",\n                \"s-startup\",\n                \"s-timeout-config\",\n                \"s-transfer\",\n                \"s-verify-api\",\n                \"s-verify-vote\",\n                \"s-vote\"\n              ]\n            },\n            \"connection\": {\n              \"explanation\": \"Log and snapshot history survive role changes, while volatile support and client futures do not transfer to a new leader generation. New authority re-establishes index support through real replication and its current-term no-op; voter log-freshness checks connect persisted history to elections. Membership is latest-versus-committed: new leader changes wait for a committed current-term entry and stable configuration, then update voter aggregation and all-peer replication; retained voter IDs preserve their slots. Followers roll back latest configuration on suffix conflict and recover configuration from snapshot/logs. Snapshot installation supplies a prefix match only after storage/FSM restore and response processing; application queueing is distinct from completed application. VerifyLeader uses a separate Boolean notification path and must not be equated with commitment. User Restore is an explicitly restricted disaster-recovery override with aborted inflight futures and a later no-op completion.\",\n              \"behavior_ids\": [\n                \"b-leader-life\",\n                \"b-config\",\n                \"b-vote\",\n                \"b-recover\",\n                \"b-install\",\n                \"b-user-restore\",\n                \"b-verify\"\n              ],\n              \"fact_ids\": [\n                \"f-match\",\n                \"f-vote-granted\",\n                \"f-verification-notification\"\n              ],\n              \"source_ids\": [\n                \"s-bootstrap\",\n                \"s-commitment\",\n                \"s-config-change\",\n                \"s-dispatch\",\n                \"s-fsm\",\n                \"s-heartbeat\",\n                \"s-install\",\n                \"s-leader-life\",\n                \"s-leader-loop\",\n                \"s-match-notify\",\n                \"s-membership-contract\",\n                \"s-repl-ownership\",\n                \"s-replication\",\n                \"s-restore-contract\",\n                \"s-rpc\",\n                \"s-snapshot-send\",\n                \"s-stable-context\",\n                \"s-startup\",\n                \"s-transfer\",\n                \"s-user-restore\",\n                \"s-verify-api\",\n                \"s-verify-vote\",\n                \"s-vote\"\n              ]\n            },\n            \"open_details\": [\n              \"Network heartbeat concurrent context-write interleavings versus main loop; source comments and wiring differ.\",\n              \"VerifyLeader suffrage filtering, response timing and applicable authority contract need discrimination.\",\n              \"Heartbeat contact versus higher-term reply handling: other workers and negative verification may protect authority.\",\n              \"Pipeline error/partial-response semantics relative to AppendFuture.Response contract.\",\n              \"Automatic snapshot creation/compaction, forced RecoverCluster and store-specific crash behavior remain deferred.\",\n              \"No executed operation history, property evidence, or overall correctness conclusion exists.\"\n            ],\n            \"core_gaps\": [],\n            \"status\": \"usable\",\n            \"rationale\": \"Source-grounded navigation of normal formation, election/context change, old-work cleanup and necessary membership/recovery/application support. Usable means sufficient initial mechanism understanding for a local question, not a correctness claim or verified fault coverage.\"\n          }\n        },\n        \"f-append-accepted\": {\n          \"before\": {},\n          \"after\": {\n            \"id\": \"f-append-accepted\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Receiver completed the append handler with Success=true for this request; new entries passed storage calls and previous-entry checks when supplied. This alone is neither quorum commitment nor FSM completion.\",\n            \"identity\": {\n              \"request\": \"Transport-associated AppendEntries request\",\n              \"history\": \"Request term and previous/log indices\"\n            },\n            \"validity_context\": \"Receiver context at handling; empty heartbeat carries no log support\",\n            \"representation\": [\n              \"AppendEntriesResponse.Success\"\n            ],\n            \"invalidators\": [],\n            \"reinterpreters\": [],\n            \"durability\": \"Reply is volatile; entry durability depends on LogStore.\",\n            \"recovery\": \"History can later be reconciled or restored from snapshot.\",\n            \"source_ids\": [\n              \"s-rpc\"\n            ],\n            \"unknowns\": [\n              \"Transport delivery and request/response correlation remain implementation-dependent.\"\n            ]\n          }\n        },\n        \"f-applied\": {\n          \"before\": {},\n          \"after\": {\n            \"id\": \"f-applied\",\n            \"meaning\": \"The FSM Apply/ApplyBatch call for a command returned and its associated future response was assigned before successful response notification.\",\n            \"identity\": {\n              \"entry\": \"log Index and Term\",\n              \"future\": \"logFuture\"\n            },\n            \"validity_context\": \"runFSM processed command tuple\",\n            \"representation\": [\n              \"logFuture.response\",\n              \"deferError.errCh\"\n            ],\n            \"invalidators\": [],\n            \"reinterpreters\": [],\n            \"durability\": \"Application durability belongs to FSM; completion itself volatile.\",\n            \"recovery\": \"FSM snapshot restoration is separate from client future recovery.\",\n            \"source_ids\": [\n              \"s-fsm\",\n              \"s-future-completion\",\n              \"s-future-contract\"\n            ],\n            \"unknowns\": []\n          }\n        },\n        \"f-commit\": {\n          \"before\": {},\n          \"after\": {\n            \"id\": \"f-commit\",\n            \"meaning\": \"Majority order statistic of accepted voter match slots passed this generation startIndex and advanced its commit index.\",\n            \"identity\": {\n              \"generation\": \"commitment object\",\n              \"prefix\": \"commitIndex\"\n            },\n            \"validity_context\": \"Current voter set at recalculation; startIndex identifies first new-term entry\",\n            \"representation\": [\n              \"commitment.commitIndex\",\n              \"commitCh notification\"\n            ],\n            \"invalidators\": [],\n            \"reinterpreters\": [],\n            \"durability\": \"Volatile aggregation; committed history retained through log/snapshot mechanisms.\",\n            \"recovery\": \"Re-established using new leader suppo