-rpc\",\n            \"s-network-dispatch\",\n            \"s-inmem-heartbeat\"\n          ],\n          \"unknowns\": [\n            \"Fast-path concurrent term transitions require a separate interleaving analysis; comments saying main-thread-only conflict with callback wiring.\"\n          ]\n        }\n      },\n      \"b-campaign\": {\n        \"before\": {},\n        \"after\": {\n          \"id\": \"b-campaign\",\n          \"primary_activity\": \"A2\",\n          \"execution_owner\": \"runFollower/runCandidate and per-voter request workers\",\n          \"protocol_context\": \"Campaign-local response channels, latest voter configuration and term\",\n          \"trigger\": \"Eligible follower timeout, retry timeout, or transfer nomination\",\n          \"legal_preconditions\": [],\n          \"implementation_guards\": [],\n          \"reads\": [],\n          \"writes\": [\n            \"Pre-vote when supported and enabled; after enough grants persist next term, self vote and dispatch RequestVote to each other voter; tally majority into Leader role.\"\n          ],\n          \"durable_effects\": [],\n          \"external_effects\": [],\n          \"important_branches\": [\n            \"Pre-vote unsupported RPC can count as grant only for preliminary round; real election still required. Higher response term demotes. Each campaign has a new buffered response channel; late old replies do not feed next tally.\",\n            \"TimeoutNow selects Candidate and transfer flag; transfer skips pre-vote and permits vote despite known leader. Sender waits for replication nextIndex beyond lastIndex before TimeoutNow.\"\n          ],\n          \"async_boundaries\": [],\n          \"produces_fact_ids\": [\n            \"f-leader-generation\"\n          ],\n          \"consumes_fact_ids\": [\n            \"f-vote-granted\"\n          ],\n          \"cross_activity_effects\": {},\n          \"existing_protections\": [\n            \"Campaign sources are selected voters; vot